alice has one of the most  interesting backstories of all of the  cullens with her father plotting to get  rid of her and throwing her in an asylum  but why didn't any of that make it into  the twilight movies  alice cullen's backstory is so  incredibly rich and interesting  that it inspired a collection of short  films the films were part of a fan  contest  and the best entry was the mary alice  brandon file  which highlighted alice's traumatic  childhood and her journey to becoming  one of the most  powerful vampires in the world as you've  gathered from the title  alice was born mary alice brandon and  her childhood was  anything but easy however those troubles  make alice's optimism and energy  even more inspiring but there are many  things that the twilight movies gloss  over when it comes to potentially the  most  interesting of all the cullen siblings  the way alice grew up gives us a deeper  look into how she developed such a close  bond with edward  and how she was able to use her visions  to become a vegetarian even before she  met her adoptive vampire family  while leaving her story out of the films  was in large part due to time  constraints  and how much work it would have taken to  tell the story properly  there are a few other issues like the  fact that alice barely remembers her  life as a human  in case you're also a bit fuzzy on what  that was like let's give a quick recap  of the life of mary alice brandon before  we get into what her story really means  to the series  and what we finally learn about her in  midnight sun  oh and if you haven't seen all the  movies or read the books there are  definite spoilers ahead  alice was born into a middle class home  in biloxi mississippi  in 1901 to a jeweler father and a  stay-at-home mom  alice had already had premonitions since  she was a child but they weren't nearly  as exact as they would become when she  turned into a vampire  people in her small town weren't big  fans of her because whenever she tried  to warn them about her unfortunate  predictions they would think her mad  and call her a wick  one day alice had a vision of her  mother's tragic passing and tried to  warn her  her mother actually believed her but her  father didn't  father it wasn't an accident enough for  your stories  eventually whoever was after her got her  and it was declared an accident  within six months alice's father  remarried a new woman who hated alice  but loved her little sister cynthia  alice had a vision of her father  planning to get rid of her  like what happened to her mother alice  rushed to the town's marshall for help  but her father had already told everyone  she was crazy  see this is what i was telling you  she's insane she ended up getting sent  to an asylum  while in the asylum she literally lost  her mind  she endured electroshock therapy which  gave her amnesia  but while there she also met a  mysterious and friendly vampire who  treated her like a daughter  he would even hide things in his hands  to test her psychic abilities  but eventually alice had another  troubling vision  this time about a powerful tracker  hunting her down  this tracker was james alice informed  her vampire friend  and realizing that there was really no  way out of this  she decided to let him change her the  vampire did and hid her away going off  to distract james but he ended up  sacrificing himself to buy alice more  time  james decided to just let her turn since  she was already well into the process  and then alice was a vampire the bite  did have some negative effects  the pain was so bad that alice lost her  memories all over again  but her premonitions were also  intensified and she saw both jasper  whitlock  and her future with the cullen family  since she had this heads up  she was able to adopt a vampiric  vegetarian lifestyle  all on her own she finally met jasper at  an empty diner in philadelphia in 1948  and helped him adopt a vegetarian  lifestyle too  and in 1950 they joined the cullens  eclipse gives fans a look into jasper  and rosalie's lives before they met  carlisle  and midnight sun gives even more insight  into what carlisle himself went through  but in terms of rich vampire backstories  that's about it explaining alice's  backstory would have meant a lot more  scenes and a lot more characters  so ultimately the film's decided not to  include it but there's enough stuff  there that alice could have had her very  own movie  as demonstrated by the short film  instead the movies focused on alice's  bond with jasper and the formation of  the cullens  alice's complicated backstory would have  given us a better sense of just  how much self-control this self-taught  vamp vegetarian really has  she literally had no one to help her  figure things out  except her own visions of the future  these visions gave her incredible  strength  and that strength is found in the will  to do hard things and steer herself  towards the right path  because she knows that that's ultimately  where she has to end up  it's easy to be upset that we never got  a good look into alice's amazing inner  strength and just how much she protects  the cullens with her visions  but it also kind of makes sense that the  movies wouldn't want to take the time to  show us all this  after all alice doesn't really remember  her life as a human so she wouldn't  really be able to discuss her past  in depth and none of the cullens were  there to witness her history  at least breaking dawn part 2 did find a  way to highlight alice's importance with  that huge vampire werewolf battle  that turned out to just be one of  alice's visions this moment gives us an  idea  of just how powerful these visions can  be and what would happen to the cullens  if they didn't have alice to point them  in the right direction  alice's story would have given us a  greater sense of her bond with edward  though  and that's probably the aspect that  would have made the most sense to  include  in the movies both alice and edward bond  over something invisible their  supernatural abilities are understated  in the sense that they can see or hear  things that no one else can  there's a huge burden that comes with  having supernatural abilities that help  them  but also take away everything that's  mysterious about life  it's the burden of knowing on top of the  burden of immortality  but even if we didn't get to see this  bond play out more explicitly in the  movies we did get some deeper insight  into how it affects edward analysis  relationship in midnight sun  the biggest revelation from midnight sun  is that edward knew pretty much from the  start that bella was  probably going to become a vampire  that's because he can read  alice's mind and see her visions which  include the possibilities of him turning  bella  leaving her or losing her completely the  way alice's visions work is by providing  all potential futures so edward and  alice work together to figure out what  could protect bella and how turning her  might actually work when edward takes  bella to the meadow  he knows that he could be overcome with  bloodlust but he's able to push through  it  this knowledge lets us finally  understand some of edward's  indecisiveness when it comes to bella  and why he always seemed so conservative  kept holding himself back and second  guessing his actions  but edward never told bella this and  didn't want alice to tell her either  so that she would still have some free  will on the flip side  this shows us that alice and edward have  very little free will of their own  if this had been included in the movies  we would have been able to see  just how much alice affected edward and  bella's relationship  and we might have further sympathized  with edward's inner turmoil  edward decides by the end of midnight  sun to live in the present  and resist the urge to peek into alice's  visions i didn't look into the future  it was enough that i could feel it  coming when i 